  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Local-first ownership",
      "items": [
        "Electron owns filesystem access; the renderer calls explicit preload APIs.",
        "Library metadata is JSON, not the sync or account SQLite database.",
        "Original media remains in user-controlled folders. Thumbnail caches are derived.",
        "The LAN service is opt-in. Pairing is public but short-lived; protected routes require a device credential."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Ingestion and recovery",
      "items": [
        "Upload offsets and job state survive restart; incoming files hold partial bytes.",
        "The importer validates type and size, computes SHA-256, and detects prior-sync duplicates.",
        "After safe storage, the injected adapter reuses indexStore.addPhoto and JSON persistence.",
        "In the pinned commit, images enter that adapter; videos are stored but skip indexing. M1 changes this in the working tree."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Current working-tree additions",
      "items": [
        "Solid topology and source links describe commit bf61edc, not uncommitted code.",
        "Native Android exists locally: Compose UI, MediaStore, WorkManager, Room queue and certificate-pinned HTTPS to the same LAN API.",
        "M1 adds expected-hash checks, library-wide duplicates and video indexing; M3 adds file history and upload-queue controls.",
        "Android and M3 are not commit-linked nodes here. iOS native sync is not implemented.",
        "Other dirty additions include branding and preview workers; this is a subsystem overview, not a file inventory."
      ]
    }
  ]
